symbol call_note
lines 0 31
hash 3e7a134056ea2869
note The guard rail: in a flow, a step belongs under the step that calls it, so a placement the call graph does not support prints a note with the tour-move command that fixes it. Only a function-like child (function, method, macro, constructor, proc) is checked, so data placed under the function that works on it is a normal step, and a step under its own symbol is not flagged. Only flows are checked; layers and data are groupings, not call trees.

